  "review_notes": [
    "Independent review identity: /root/review_gate/kernel/reviewer-main__melee__cm__cmsnap-1. Reviewed the current top-level proposal.json, not merely the prior librarian packet. Read proposal.json lines 1\u2013181, functionality.md lines 1\u201330, fact-dispositions.json lines 1\u2013370, and link-dispositions.json lines 1\u2013334.",
    "All seven proposed writes are supported and address owned subjects. Five replace baseline facts; two document previously fact-free callback parameters. No entities, merges, follow-ups, or new links are proposed.",
    "Canonical source confirms a singleton request/copy/delay/consume protocol. Four active callback invocations reach Unk5: one copying invocation and three bounded increments. This establishes software eligibility, not a hardware completion query or exact frame cadence.",
    "Independently checked CmSnapStatus, both assertion macro branches, image initialization and copy helpers, GObj construction/registration/destruction, and the active Camera Mode table, dispatchers, request, polling, and initialization callers. Pinned symbol search returned no additional external cmsnap call sites.",
    "The proposal correctly uses snap_image rather than stale x1C, distinguishes optional preloaded storage from fallback allocation, distinguishes rounded allocation size from pointer alignment, and avoids claiming that clearing a stored pointer invalidates previously returned pointer copies.",
    "Boundary review confirms terminal-null consumption, no mutation on nonterminal or invalid-status polling, default no-op callback behavior, unused callback arguments, no local repeated-initialization guard, and unchecked nullable GObj creation. There are no TU floating-point inputs; descriptor LOD initialization uses finite zero.",
    "Retained inferred names are descriptive hypotheses only. Eight section-attached facts and two section-attached links remain explicitly unresolved. Acceptance does not resolve compiled layout, archive ownership, teardown, or GPU timing."
  ],
